HeaderInclude
config/lvx/lvx-opts.h

ffixed-reg
Target RejectNegative Joined Var(lvx_deferred_options) Defer
Set the passed register range as fixed

fstack-limit-register=
Common RejectNegative Joined Var(lvx_deferred_options) Defer

fstack-limit-symbol=
Common RejectNegative Joined Var(lvx_deferred_options) Defer

fshaker-seed=
Target RejectNegative Joined Var(lvx_deferred_options) Defer

march=
Target RejectNegative Joined Enum(lvx_arch_type) Var(lvx_arch_name) Init(LVX_ARCH_LVX_1)
-march=ARCHITECTURE  Compile for specified ARCHITECTURE

Enum
Name(lvx_arch_type) Type(enum lvx_arch_type)
Known LVX architecture types (for use with the -march option):

EnumValue
Enum(lvx_arch_type) String(lvx-1) Value(LVX_ARCH_LVX_1)

EnumValue
Enum(lvx_arch_type) String(lvx-2) Value(LVX_ARCH_LVX_2)

mfarcall
Target Var(LVX_FARCALL)
Assume every callee lies outside CALL's reach and emit the extended CALLX form

mdump-costs
Target Var(DUMP_COSTS) Init(0)
Dump calls to target-dependent cost functions

fhwloop
Target Mask(HWLOOP)
Enable hardware loop code generation when optimizing (active by default)

fdual-bcu
Target Mask(DUAL_BCU)
Enable dual BCU code generation when optimizing (active by default)

fdual-lsu
Target Mask(DUAL_LSU)
Enable dual LSU code generation when optimizing (active by default)

fsched2-dates
Target Mask(SCHED2_DATES)
Display sched2 schedule dates in assembly output (active by default)

fdivmod0-trap
Target Mask(DIVMOD0_TRAP)
Trigger trap in case of integer division/modulus by zero (active by default).

fstrict-align
Target Mask(STRICT_ALIGN)
Do not generate misaligned memory accesses 

fstack-check-use-tls
Target RejectNegative Mask(STACK_CHECK_USE_TLS)
Use a TLS slot named __stack_end to store the stack boundary instead of $sr1

mabi=
Target RejectNegative Joined Enum(lvx_abi) Var(lvx_abi) Init(LVX_ABI_DEFAULT)
-mabi=ABI	Generate code that conforms to the specified ABI

Enum
Name(lvx_abi) Type(int)
Known LVX Machine ABIs (for use with the -mabi= option):

Waddress-space-conversion
C Warning Var(LVX_WARN_ADDRESS_SPACE_CONVERSION) Init(0)
Warn if an __bypass pointer is converted to a general one or vice versa

EnumValue
Enum(lvx_abi) String(lp64) Value(LVX_ABI_LP64)

; Only lvx.cc reads this, so it lives here.  Optimization makes it per
; function, and lvx_machine_dependent_reorg gates it on speed as well.
msuperblock-loops
Target Var(lvx_superblock_loops) Init(1) Optimization
Lay inner loop bodies out as one superblock run before EBB scheduling.

munfold-inner-loops
Target Var(lvx_unfold_inner_loops) Init(0) Optimization
Duplicate the body of an inner loop that is not a hardware loop, so the extended basic block is twice as long.  Implies -mregrename-inner-loops.

munfold-max-blocks=
Target RejectNegative Joined UInteger Var(lvx_unfold_max_blocks) Init(8) Optimization
-munfold-max-blocks=N	Do not unfold an inner loop whose body has more than N blocks.

munfold-max-insns=
Target RejectNegative Joined UInteger Var(lvx_unfold_max_insns) Init(64) Optimization
-munfold-max-insns=N	Do not unfold an inner loop whose body has more than N instructions.

mregrename-inner-loops
Target Var(lvx_regrename_inner_loops_p) Init(0) Optimization
Rename registers through inner superblock loops before EBB scheduling, so successive definitions use different registers.

munfold-min-gain=
Target RejectNegative Joined UInteger Var(lvx_unfold_min_gain) Init(10) Optimization
-munfold-min-gain=N	Do not unfold an inner loop unless the predicted saving is at least N percent.

mcms-probe
Target Var(lvx_cms_probe) Init(0) Optimization
Dump the convergent-modulo-scheduling probe for each measured inner loop.

mcms-release=
Target RejectNegative Joined UInteger Var(lvx_cms_release_policy) Init(1) Optimization
-mcms-release=N	SWO release-date policy: 0 none, 1 every unblamed task with slack to its ALAP, 2 only culprits of resource contention, 3 culprits damped by accumulated guilt, 4 every task with slack, 5 Huff's stretchable-side decision, which releases an operation only when it has more values to stretch forward than backward.

mcms-split-wide=
Target RejectNegative Joined UInteger Var(lvx_cms_split_wide) Init(0) Optimization
-mcms-split-wide=N	How a lifetime-splitting copy of a value wider than one register is costed: 0 one COPYD per register (TINY each), 1 prefer CATDQ (one per 128 bits, costing a LITE and a TINY).

mcms-load-latency=
Target RejectNegative Joined UInteger Var(lvx_cms_load_latency) Init(15) Optimization
-mcms-load-latency=N	Charge every load N cycles of latency instead of what the machine description gives, 0 uses the description, and the default of 15 is the uncached .us variant, which is the regime to design for.

mcms-regalloc-feasible
Target Var(lvx_cms_regalloc_feasible) Init(0) Optimization
Reject an initiation interval whose modulo kernel cannot be register allocated, making colourability a feasibility test inside the II search rather than a property discovered afterwards.

mcms-exact-degree
Target Var(lvx_cms_exact_degree) Init(0) Optimization
Colour the interference graph with exact modulo expansion degrees instead of degrees rounded up to a power of two, to separate the cost of the rounding from the cost of the schedule.

mcms-stage-sched
Target Var(lvx_cms_stage_sched) Init(0) Optimization
After a modulo schedule converges, shift operations by whole multiples of the initiation interval to shorten live ranges, which changes the stage but not the modulo cycle and so cannot affect resources or the initiation interval (Eichenberger's skip factors).

mcms-ii-bias=
Target RejectNegative Joined UInteger Var(lvx_cms_ii_bias) Init(0) Optimization
-mcms-ii-bias=N	Start the initiation-interval search N cycles above the lower bound, to compare schedulers at an II neither of them would have chosen.

mcms-branch-stage=
Target RejectNegative Joined UInteger Var(lvx_cms_branch_stage) Init(3) Optimization
-mcms-branch-stage=N	Release-date floor for the loop-back branch, to push it into the last stage and so remove the partial epilogues an early prologue exit needs: 0 none, 1 its ALAP, 2 the last stage of the dependence-only makespan, 3 as 1 but retried unpinned at the same II so the pin never costs II.

mcms-priority=
Target RejectNegative Joined UInteger Var(lvx_cms_priority) Init(1) Optimization
-mcms-priority=N	List-scheduling priority: 0 longest path from source (ASAP), 1 longest path to sink (default), 2 lowest slack first.

mcms-swo-budget=
Target RejectNegative Joined UInteger Var(lvx_cms_swo_budget) Init(4) Optimization
-mcms-swo-budget=N	Allow N squeaky-wheel passes at each candidate initiation interval before trying the next.  One is a single greedy construction, the pre-SWO behaviour.

mcms-inductive-relaxation
Target Var(lvx_cms_inductive_relaxation) Init(0) Optimization
Drop scheduling arcs from a simple induction's definition to its uses as a base+displacement base, assuming codegen adjusts the displacements.

mcms-stride-test
Target Var(lvx_cms_stride_test) Init(1) Optimization
Disprove cross-iteration memory dependences whose addresses are affine in the iteration number with a common stride.

mcms-max-insns=
Target RejectNegative Joined UInteger Var(lvx_cms_max_insns) Init(256) Optimization
-mcms-max-insns=N	Do not consider an inner loop with more than N instructions for modulo scheduling.

mcms-force-speculative-loads
Target Var(lvx_cms_force_spec_loads) Init(0) Optimization
Emit loop-variant-address loads in pipelined inner loops as their dismissible variant.

mcms-assume-ivdep
Target Var(lvx_cms_assume_ivdep) Init(0) Optimization
Assume every inner loop carries #pragma GCC ivdep; for measurement only, not a legal transformation.

mcms-mcrl-release=
Target RejectNegative Joined UInteger Var(lvx_cms_mcrl_release) Init(0) Optimization
-mcms-mcrl-release=N	Seed the SWO release dates from the minimum cumulative register lifetime solution: 0 off, 1 the first construction only, 2 as a persistent base the release policy diversifies around.
